+// A QUANTIZED CONVOLUTION KERNEL, AND WHY IT COSTS ONE DEQUANTIZE AND NOTHING ELSE
+//
+// ggml lays quantization blocks along ne[0]. For a conv kernel stored the way it is declared --
+// [KW, KH, IC, OC] -- ne[0] is the kernel WIDTH, 1, 3, 5 or 7, and no block size divides that. So a
+// producer that wants a block-quantized convolution folds the kernel's spatial and input-channel axes
+// into ne[0] first, giving [IC*KH*KW, OC], and hands the erased geometry back on the node
+// (ggml_conv_2d_direct_packed, op_params 6..8). A folded kernel and a declared one are then
+// indistinguishable by shape, which is why the geometry is READ rather than inferred.
+//
+// What makes this cheap is that the direct sweep below never reads the kernel as stored: it repacks
+// the whole thing into an F32 scratch buffer (`wp`) before computing anything, and the register-tiled
+// inner kernel reads only that. So a quantized kernel needs no quantized inner loop, no vec_dot and no
+// activation quantized to vec_dot_type -- it needs ONE dequantize into a buffer of the same shape, and
+// everything below is untouched: the direct sweep, the phase-major variant, the batched im2col
+// fallback, the bias/leaky/residual fusions, the thread splits.
+//
+// It is also more accurate than a quantized dot would be: dequantize-then-F32-FMA against a Q8_0
+// activation dot. And it costs, over ALL 59.5 MB of a VITS vocoder's convolution weights at once,
+// 10.3 ms against the 8.5 ms F32 pack it replaces -- +1.8 ms on a ~500 ms synthesis (scripts/bench21.c
+// in the loom tree). The pack loop reads LESS memory in the quantized case (8.4 MB of Q4_0 rather than
+// 59.5 MB of F32) and writes the same amount, so the delta is arithmetic rather than traffic.
+//
+// The one thing it is NOT right for is a convolution inside a decode loop, where the dequantize would
+// be paid per token rather than per utterance. Nothing in ggml routes SSM_CONV here.
+
+// The folded geometry a CONV_2D node may carry, or the declared one off the kernel's own ne. A zero
+// `kw` in op_params 6 is what says "declared", which is every graph that never folded anything.
+static bool ggml_conv_2d_packed_geometry(const ggml_tensor * dst, const ggml_tensor * kernel,
+                                         int64_t * kw, int64_t * kh, int64_t * ic, int64_t * oc) {
+    const int32_t pkw = ggml_get_op_params_i32(dst, 6);
